 ],
 "notes": "Armory modal, Spells tab selected (tab.spells has the lit gold frame, warmer label colour and diamond finials top/bottom; the other four tabs are idle navy). Header subtitle reads 'EQUIPPED 4 / 5' and is split into a caption and a dynamic count because the concept's word spacing is wider than Cinzel's. Equipped strip: slots 1-4 hold Fireball and three other spells (blue shield, green chalice, purple lightning), each Lv 1 with 1 of 4 pips filled; slot 1 is the selected slot (glowing orange frame); slot 5 is empty (grey plus + 'Empty slot', no class icon/level/pips). Number badges are gold plates in each slot's top-left corner with black serif numerals; the concept numerals are taller and narrower than Crimson (ink about 17 px tall), so the width-fitted size draws them shorter. Spell collection: 3-column grid, 10 spells, all Lv 1; grid.0.0 (Fireball) is selected with the same orange glow frame. Pip rows are right-aligned 10 px from the cell edge and show 3 diamonds on some cells and 2 on others (1 filled each), so the count varies per spell. Cell sizes are slightly irregular in the concept (rows 86/84/82 tall, columns 98/93/96 wide); row 3 is clipped by the panel bottom (only grid.3.0 is visible, pips hidden), so the grid scrolls. Scrollbar: thin gold track with a two-segment lighter thumb at the top (thumb at scroll position 0). Preview well shows the hero casting the selected spell on a pedestal, with prev/next chevrons. Detail column has no frame (wood on the left, parchment map with lantern/chests on the right): flame icon + 'Fireball', 'Lv 1' with 1 of 4 pips, a translucent chip (flame medallion + 'Damage \u00b7 Area' with a crosshair icon), a thin gold rule fading out to the right, a one-line description, four stat tiles (2x2, icon left, caption + value) and two buttons: BACK (navy) and SCRIBE 134 (gold, primary, dark label plus a coin pile icon). SCRIBE and its cost are separate text elements because the concept puts a wider gap before the number."
}